    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "vil gjerne + verb",
      "text": "After \"vil\" the next verb stays in its basic form, which usually ends in -e: \"snakke\" (speak), \"bo\" (live). You have seen the -er form: Sam snakker, Sam bor. \"Jeg vil gjerne …\" is a friendly way to say \"I would like to …\". After \"liker\" the basic form comes with the little word \"å\": \"liker å snakke norsk\".",
